1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:08,300
After he had finished all his sayings in the hearing of the people, he entered Capernaum.

2
00:00:08,820 --> 00:00:15,540
Now a centurion had a servant who was sick and at the point of death, who was highly valued by him.

3
00:00:16,120 --> 00:00:23,220
When the centurion heard about Jesus, he sent to him elders of the Jews, asking him to come and heal his servant.

4
00:00:23,900 --> 00:00:28,180
And when they came to Jesus, they pleaded with him earnestly, saying,

5
00:00:28,180 --> 00:00:36,220
He is worthy to have you do this for him, for he loves our nation, and he is the one who built us our synagogue.

6
00:00:37,040 --> 00:00:38,380
And Jesus went with them.

7
00:00:39,040 --> 00:00:44,500
When he was not far from the house, the centurion sent friends, saying to him,

8
00:00:45,140 --> 00:00:50,560
Lord, do not trouble yourself, for I am not worthy to have you come under my roof.

9
00:00:51,340 --> 00:00:57,020
Therefore I did not presume to come to you, but say the word and let my servant be healed.

10
00:00:57,020 --> 00:01:02,060
For I, too, am a man set under authority, with soldiers under me.

11
00:01:02,420 --> 00:01:05,060
And I say to one, Go, and he goes.

12
00:01:05,420 --> 00:01:08,240
And to another, Come, and he comes.

13
00:01:08,580 --> 00:01:11,660
And to my servant, Do this, and he does it.

14
00:01:12,100 --> 00:01:17,280
When Jesus heard these things, he marveled at him, and turning to the crowd that followed him, said,

15
00:01:17,960 --> 00:01:22,700
I tell you, not even in Israel have I found such faith.

16
00:01:23,100 --> 00:01:26,200
And when those who had been sent returned to the house,

17
00:01:26,460 --> 00:01:27,000
they found that they had been sent to the house, and they had been sent to the house,

18
00:01:27,000 --> 00:01:28,100
and they had found the servant well.

19
00:01:29,080 --> 00:01:32,220
Soon afterward he went to a town called Nain,

20
00:01:32,700 --> 00:01:35,320
and his disciples and a great crowd went with him.

21
00:01:36,080 --> 00:01:41,340
As he drew near to the gate of the town, behold, a man who had died was being carried out,

22
00:01:41,740 --> 00:01:44,680
the only son of his mother, and she was a widow,

23
00:01:45,120 --> 00:01:48,140
and a considerable crowd from the town was with her.

24
00:01:48,800 --> 00:01:52,920
And when the Lord saw her, he had compassion on her, and said to her,

25
00:01:53,460 --> 00:01:54,720
Do not weep.

26
00:01:55,220 --> 00:01:56,980
Then he came up and touched the beard,

27
00:01:57,000 --> 00:02:00,100
and the bearers stood still, and he said,

28
00:02:00,560 --> 00:02:04,220
Young man, I say to you, Arise.

29
00:02:05,040 --> 00:02:09,840
And the dead man sat up and began to speak, and Jesus gave him to his mother.

30
00:02:10,760 --> 00:02:14,680
Fear seized them all, and they glorified God, saying,

31
00:02:15,360 --> 00:02:20,680
A great prophet has arisen among us, and God has visited his people.

32
00:02:21,040 --> 00:02:26,840
And this report about him spread through the whole of Judea and all the surrounding country,

33
00:02:27,760 --> 00:02:29,640
And these are the assertions of the disciples where,

34
00:02:29,800 --> 00:02:31,500
And I have included here the portrait of the father,

35
00:02:31,660 --> 00:02:32,600
and my answer to them.

36
00:02:33,560 --> 00:02:34,320
directly decline

37
00:02:34,320 --> 00:02:35,520
before the father is incarnated,

38
00:02:35,520 --> 00:02:37,880
and is based upon the bosom of his mother.

39
00:02:38,660 --> 00:02:39,880
The disciples of John reported

40
00:02:39,880 --> 00:02:41,360
all these things to him,

41
00:02:41,860 --> 00:02:45,040
and John, calling two of his disciples to him,

42
00:02:45,040 --> 00:02:47,080
sent them to the Lord, saying,

43
00:02:47,080 --> 00:02:49,320
Are you the one who is to come,

44
00:02:49,320 --> 00:02:51,500
or shall we look for another?

45
00:02:51,960 --> 00:02:54,560
And when the men had come to him, they said,

46
00:02:54,560 --> 00:02:56,560
John, the Baptist, has sent us to you, saying,

47
00:02:56,560 --> 00:03:00,840
And on many who were blind he bestowed sight, and he answered them,

48
00:03:01,580 --> 00:03:03,880
Go, and tell John what you have seen and heard.

49
00:03:04,380 --> 00:03:09,580
The blind receive their sight, the lame walk, lepers are cleansed, and the deaf hear.

50
00:03:10,100 --> 00:03:13,760
The dead are raised up, the poor have good news preached to them.

51
00:03:14,460 --> 00:03:17,700
And blessed is the one who is not offended by me.

52
00:03:18,260 --> 00:03:23,860
When John's messengers had gone, Jesus began to speak to the crowds concerning John.

53
00:03:23,860 --> 00:03:27,220
What did you go out into the wilderness to see?

54
00:03:27,560 --> 00:03:29,440
A reed shaken by the wind.

55
00:03:30,400 --> 00:03:32,180
What then did you go out to see?

56
00:03:32,580 --> 00:03:34,520
A man dressed in soft clothing?

57
00:03:35,400 --> 00:03:40,720
Behold, those who are dressed in splendid clothing and live in luxury are in king's courts.

58
00:03:41,580 --> 00:03:43,340
What then did you go out to see?

59
00:03:43,720 --> 00:03:44,260
A prophet?

60
00:03:45,040 --> 00:03:47,840
Yes, I tell you, and more than a prophet.

61
00:03:48,460 --> 00:03:50,200
This is he of whom it is written,

62
00:03:50,900 --> 00:03:53,840
Behold, I send my messenger before you,

63
00:03:53,860 --> 00:03:56,960
who will prepare your way before you.

64
00:03:57,680 --> 00:04:02,540
I tell you, among those born of women, none is greater than John,

65
00:04:02,920 --> 00:04:07,140
yet the one who is least in the kingdom of God is greater than he.

66
00:04:07,860 --> 00:04:11,980
When all the people heard this, and the tax collectors too,

67
00:04:12,420 --> 00:04:17,160
they declared God just, having been baptized with the baptism of John.

68
00:04:17,520 --> 00:04:21,700
But the Pharisees and the lawyers rejected the purpose of God for themselves.

69
00:04:22,020 --> 00:04:23,600
Not having been baptized,

70
00:04:23,600 --> 00:04:28,340
To what then shall I compare the people of this generation?

71
00:04:29,000 --> 00:04:30,380
And what are they like?

72
00:04:31,180 --> 00:04:35,380
They are like children sitting in the marketplace and calling to one another.

73
00:04:35,920 --> 00:04:38,900
We played the flute for you, and you did not dance.

74
00:04:39,360 --> 00:04:42,140
We sing a dirge, and you did not weep.

75
00:04:42,680 --> 00:04:46,280
For John the Baptist has come eating no bread and drinking no wine,

76
00:04:46,560 --> 00:04:48,600
and you say, He has a demon.

77
00:04:49,320 --> 00:04:52,100
The Son of Man has come eating and drinking, and you say,

78
00:04:52,280 --> 00:04:53,320
Look at him!

79
00:04:53,320 --> 00:04:57,520
A glutton and a drunkard, a friend of tax collectors and sinners.

80
00:04:58,880 --> 00:05:02,240
Yet wisdom is justified by all her children.

81
00:05:04,240 --> 00:05:06,800
One of the Pharisees asked him to eat with him,

82
00:05:07,060 --> 00:05:10,260
and he went into the Pharisee's house and took his place at the table.

83
00:05:11,000 --> 00:05:14,300
And behold, a woman of the city, who was a sinner,

84
00:05:14,800 --> 00:05:18,300
when she learned that he was reclining at table in the Pharisee's house,

85
00:05:18,960 --> 00:05:21,240
brought an alabaster flask of ointment,

86
00:05:21,620 --> 00:05:23,300
and standing behind him,

87
00:05:23,720 --> 00:05:27,420
she began to wet his feet with her tears,

88
00:05:27,820 --> 00:05:30,080
and wiped them with the hair of her head,

89
00:05:30,540 --> 00:05:31,640
and kissed his feet,

90
00:05:31,960 --> 00:05:33,540
and anointed them with the ointment.

91
00:05:34,420 --> 00:05:37,260
Now when the Pharisee who had invited him saw this,

92
00:05:37,760 --> 00:05:38,900
he said to himself,

93
00:05:39,440 --> 00:05:41,400
If this man were a prophet,

94
00:05:41,660 --> 00:05:47,040
he would have known who and what sort of woman this is who is touching him,

95
00:05:47,360 --> 00:05:49,380
for she is a sinner.

96
00:05:50,260 --> 00:05:52,300
And Jesus answering said to him,

97
00:05:52,440 --> 00:05:52,960
Son of Man,

98
00:05:52,960 --> 00:05:55,920
Simon, I have something to say to you.

99
00:05:56,540 --> 00:05:57,540
And he answered,

100
00:05:58,340 --> 00:05:59,500
Say it, teacher.

101
00:06:00,320 --> 00:06:02,380
A certain moneylender had two debtors.

102
00:06:02,880 --> 00:06:06,300
One owed five hundred denarii, and the other fifty.

103
00:06:07,040 --> 00:06:09,920
When they could not pay, he cancelled the debt of both.

104
00:06:10,660 --> 00:06:13,100
Now which of them will love him more?

105
00:06:13,940 --> 00:06:14,840
Simon answered,

106
00:06:15,640 --> 00:06:20,800
The one, I suppose, for whom he cancelled the larger debt.

107
00:06:20,800 --> 00:06:22,580
And he said to him,

108
00:06:22,960 --> 00:06:25,040
You have judged rightly.

109
00:06:25,780 --> 00:06:28,280
Then turning toward the woman, he said to Simon,

110
00:06:28,880 --> 00:06:30,220
Do you see this woman?

111
00:06:31,040 --> 00:06:32,420
I entered your house.

112
00:06:32,680 --> 00:06:34,700
You gave me no water for my feet,

113
00:06:35,280 --> 00:06:38,120
but she has wet my feet with her tears,

114
00:06:38,380 --> 00:06:39,840
and wiped them with her hair.

115
00:06:40,540 --> 00:06:42,180
You gave me no kiss,

116
00:06:42,660 --> 00:06:44,340
but from the time I came in,

117
00:06:44,440 --> 00:06:46,780
she has not ceased to kiss my feet.

118
00:06:47,380 --> 00:06:49,520
You did not anoint my head with oil,

119
00:06:49,520 --> 00:06:52,800
but she has anointed my feet with ointment,

120
00:06:53,480 --> 00:06:55,200
therefore I tell you,

121
00:06:55,620 --> 00:06:58,220
her sins, which are many, are forgiven,

122
00:06:58,880 --> 00:07:00,360
for she loved much.

123
00:07:01,220 --> 00:07:04,400
But he who is forgiven little, loves little.

124
00:07:05,160 --> 00:07:06,140
And he said to her,

125
00:07:06,840 --> 00:07:08,840
Your sins are forgiven.

126
00:07:09,700 --> 00:07:12,920
Then those who were at table with him began to say among themselves,

127
00:07:13,720 --> 00:07:17,140
Who is this, who even forgives sins?

128
00:07:17,600 --> 00:07:19,180
And he said to the woman,

129
00:07:19,580 --> 00:07:21,900
Your faith has saved you.

130
00:07:22,480 --> 00:07:22,820
Go,

131
00:07:22,960 --> 00:07:23,640
in peace.

132
00:07:23,640 --> 00:07:23,800
Go,

133
00:07:23,800 --> 00:07:23,840
in peace.

